<td id="A2.T10.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_tttt" colspan="12">
<span id="A2.T10.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:155.3pt;">
<span id="A2.T10.2.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.T10.2.4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example Question 2:</span> 
<br class="ltx_break">What is Elizabeth’s opinion of Mr. Darcy? 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A2.T10.2.4.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Source: Pride and Prejudice</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A2.T10.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tttt" colspan="9">
<span id="A2.T10.2.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:155.3pt;">
<span id="A2.T10.2.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">(A) He is proud and disagreeable. 
<br class="ltx_break">(B) She is ashamed of her prejudice and feels respect for him. 
<br class="ltx_break">(C) She loves him. 
<br class="ltx_break">(D) He is a dishonest man who does not keep his word. 
<br class="ltx_break">(E) She is offended by his perception of her. 
<br class="ltx_break">(F) The question cannot be answered at this point in the story.</span>
</span></td></tr>
