<span id="A2.T10.2.7.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:155.3pt;">
<span id="A2.T10.2.7.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.T10.2.7.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example Question 3:</span> 
<br class="ltx_break">What is Victor Frankenstein’s primary goal or motivation at this point in the story? 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A2.T10.2.7.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Source: Frankenstein</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A2.T10.2.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tttt" colspan="9">
<span id="A2.T10.2.7.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:155.3pt;">
<span id="A2.T10.2.7.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">(A) To learn the secrets of nature and, specifically, the principle of life. 
<br class="ltx_break">(B) To escape the memory and consequences of his work. 
<br class="ltx_break">(C) To destroy the Monster as an act of vengeance. 
<br class="ltx_break">(D) Recovering from his illness 
<br class="ltx_break">(E) Living in regret and remorse because his creation murdered his brother William. 
<br class="ltx_break">(F) To create a companion for the Monster. 
<br class="ltx_break">(G) The question cannot be answered at this point in the story.</span>
</span></td></tr>
